course: dictionary
lesson: 7216
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. Phoenix is a good example. The words around it, and whether it has a capital letter, tell you which meaning the writer wants.
explain: «A boy in Phoenix gets a call from an unknown number.» Phoenix has a capital P and is in the middle of a sentence, so it is a name. It is the name of a place, a city, so it is a proper noun. Proper nouns always start with a capital letter.
explain: Now look at the small p. A phoenix is a magical bird from old stories. Try the meaning in the sentence: if the bird idea does not fit, you have the wrong meaning. Ask yourself: is this a place, or a creature?
explain: Sometimes a word is used as a picture. «Rise like a phoenix from the ashes» does not mean a real bird. It means to come back stronger after you have lost everything.
fact: A phoenix is a magical bird from old stories that burns itself in fire and is born again from its own ashes.
fact: Phoenix with a capital P is the capital city of the US state of Arizona, in a hot desert.
fact: In stories, a phoenix is a symbol of starting again after something terrible.
fact: In Harry Potter, Fawkes is a phoenix.
fact: «Rise like a phoenix from the ashes» means to come back stronger after failing or losing everything.
exercise: «A boy in Phoenix gets a call from an unknown number.» What is Phoenix here? | A kind of telephone | *A city | A bird from old stories | A fire that burns
exercise: «Rise like a phoenix from the ashes» is a picture. What does it mean? | To fly up into the sky | To move to a new city | To cook food over a fire | *To come back stronger after losing everything
exercise: Why does Phoenix start with a capital letter in «a girl in Phoenix»? | Because it is always the first word of a sentence | Because it is a long word | *Because it is the name of a place | Because it means a magical bird
test: «Ireland... lives at Áras an Uachtaráin in Phoenix Park, Dublin.» Here, Phoenix is part of what? | A hot desert in America | *A place name in Dublin | A magical bird | A kind of slide
test: In Harry Potter, what is Fawkes? | *A phoenix | A hippogriff | A dragon | A unicorn
exam: «The phoenix rose from the ashes.» Which meaning fits best here? | A park in Dublin | A hot metal slide | A city in Arizona | *A magical bird from old stories
